Material taken from Twelve:

  src/TGBackgroundSession.m
  third_party/tdlib/td/td/telegram/net/Session.cpp
      The selective VoIP socket policy, from
      submodules/MTProtoKit/MTProtoKit/MTTcpConnection.m
      (-socket:didConnectToHost:port:). Only the long-lived primary data
      connection is promoted to a VoIP stream and given SO_KEEPALIVE with
      TCP_KEEPALIVE set to 60 seconds; media and download sockets are never
      marked, because marking them disturbed scrolling.

  src/TGNotificationManager.m
      The iOS 6 local-notification burst control, from
      Telegraph/TGApplyUpdatesActor.mm
      (TGIOS6ConsumeLocalNotificationBudget and
      +presentSafeLocalNotification:text:). The first message of a burst wins
      and the following second folds into it, at most one sound plays every
      three seconds, an aggregate banner blocks further banners for ten
      seconds, and a hard budget of five banners per ten seconds applies,
      because iOS 6 can stall SpringBoard under a large update burst.

  src/TGClient.m
      The deferred-UI-update pattern, from legacy/TelegraphKit/TGDatabase.mm
      (TGIOS6ShouldDeferDatabaseUiUpdates and the deferred replay). Updates
      are ingested in full while the application is not active, but the chat
      list rebuild is held back and replayed as one batch when the
      application becomes active again.

  src/TGCall.mm
      The call audio-session latency setting, from Telegraph/TGCallSession.mm.
      The preferred IO buffer duration is pinned to 5 ms while a call is up
      and released back to the system default on teardown, because the iOS 6
      default buffer adds audible latency to a voice call.

  src/TGStoriesViewController.m
      The poster-frame selection, from Telegraph/TGVideoThumbnailDataSource.m
      (TGIOS6VideoFrameImage and TGIOS6ImageLooksBlack). The first frame of a
      recorded video is frequently still black, so several candidate times are
      tried and the first frame that is not almost entirely black wins, with
      the first decoded frame kept as a fallback.

  src/TGEmoji.m
      src/TGReactionPickerView.m
      The explicit emoji-font selection, from
      Telegraph/TGModernConversationController.mm. UIKit's system font on
      iOS 6 does not perform emoji fallback for every newer glyph even when an
      updated AppleColorEmoji font is installed, so labels that carry emoji
      ask for AppleColorEmoji by name and fall back to the system font only
      when that face cannot be resolved.

